kie Sports Shop Apparel, clothing, gear and\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tmerchandise Hokie Shop University Bookstore,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tmerchandise and gifts Hokie Gear Everything you need to know about Hokie gear Hokie\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLicense Plates Part of every Virginia Tech plate purchase\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfunds\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tscholarships Resources for Future Students Current Students Parents and Families Faculty and Staff Alumni Industry and Partners Search Search query × search Search this site Search all vt.edu sites People search Frequent Searches: Web results for Sort by relevance Sort by date News results for Sort by relevance Sort by date Filter search Categories Academics Campus Experience Culture Impact Research Story type Feature Notice Story Video Apply filters Clear filters Video results for Sort by relevance Sort by date People results for People Results See more VT News Results See more Office of the Executive Vice President and Provost / Faculty Affairs / Academic Personnel / Recruitment / Dual Career Program / Explore Work-Life Liaisons Current page: Dual Career Program Welcome to Dual Career! Dual Career Candidates Job Search Resources Helpful VT Job Search Tips Zoom Interview Tips Community & Networking Volunteer & Nonprofit Guidelines for Department Heads Steps for Department Heads Frequently Asked Questions Senior Administrator Search Information Dual Career Program Close lightbox dialog Previous slide Next slide Virginia Tech recognizes that dual-career considerations are a critical factor in faculty recruitment, retention, and long-term success. Today’s teaching and research faculty are often part of professional partnerships in which both individuals seek meaningful and fulfilling career opportunities. Institutions that thoughtfully address these needs are better positioned to attract exceptional faculty, support their families, and sustain a thriving academic community. Housed within the Office of the Vice Provost for Faculty Affairs, Virginia Tech’s Dual Career Program provides specialized support for the spouses and partners of teaching and research (T&R) faculty who are navigating employment transitions as part of a faculty recruitment or retention process. The program is designed to offer guidance, resources, and individualized support while setting clear and transparent expectations. Our Approach The Dual Career Program offers support, information, and strategic guidance to spouses and partners as they explore employment opportunities and integrate into their new local community. While the program actively assists individuals in identifying and pursuing career pathways, participation in the program does not guarantee employment at Virginia Tech or with external organizations. Our role is to serve as a knowledgeable partner in the job search process, helping individuals understand the regional employment landscape, refine their materials and strategies, and make informed decisions about next steps. Program goals Strengthen Virginia Tech’s ability to recruit and retain outstanding teaching and research (T&R) faculty Support faculty success by addressing the professional needs of their spouses and partners Provide personalized, confidential guidance tailored to individual career goals and circumstances Foster connections with employers, civic and volunteer organizations, and networking opportunities across the New River Valley and Roanoke Valley regions Eligibility Recruitment Support Dual career assistance is available to spouses and partners of newly recruited teaching and research faculty during the faculty member’s first year of employment at Virginia Tech. Retention Support When requested by a department head or dean, dual career resources may be made available to support retention-related needs. Services and Support The Dual Career Program provides individualized assistance that may include: Guidance in identifying employment opportunities within Virginia Tech, across the New River Valley and Roanoke Valley regions, and other Virginia Tech campuses and locations Support in developing effective job search strategies Assistance with resumes, cover letters, and other professional documents Career exploration and goal clarification Job coaching and mock interviews Information on networking strategies, professional organizations, and volunteer opportunities Relocation and community resources Confidential consultation and advising Serving as a liaison when appropriate, including outreach and communication with departments or external employers Recognizing that each individual’s situation and goals are unique, the Dual Career Program works collaboratively with participants to tailor support to their specific needs. Dual Career Candidates General Item Dual Career Candidates General Resources General Item Welcome to Dual Career! General Item Job Search Resources General Item Helpful VT Job Search Tips General Item Zoom Interview Tips Blacksburg, NRV, & Roanoke Resources General Item Community & Networking General Item Volunteer & Nonprofit Department Heads, Chairs, and Program Directors Resources General Item Guidelines for Department Heads General Item Steps for Department Heads Additional Resources General Item Moving and Relocation Resources General Item Work-Life Liaisons Article Item Jump-starting a spouse's job search with the Dual Career Program , article Register Now Meet Anna LoMascolo Senior Director of Work-Life Initiatives Dual Career Office of the Vice Provost for Faculty Affairs Burruss Hall, Suite 330 (0164), Virginia Tech 800 Drillfield Drive Blacksburg, VA 24061 dualcareers@vt.edu View our brochure for more information about the Dual Career Program Contact Us Office of the Vice Provost for Faculty Affairs Burruss Hall, Suite 330 (0164), Virginia Tech 800 Drillfield Drive Blacksburg, VA 24061 540-231-6670 facultyaffairs@vt.edu Events & Important Dates View All Events View Important Dates Get Directions See All Locations Conta