cademics Campus Experience Culture Impact Research Story type Feature Notice Story Video Apply filters Clear filters Video results for Sort by relevance Sort by date People results for People Results See more VT News Results See more Virginia Tech Jobs / Moving and Relocation Resources / Greater Washington, D.C., area / Explore Search all Virginia Tech jobs Employees only: Internal postings Committed to Our Veterans and Military Dual Career Program Employment Process Frequently Asked Questions Moving and Relocation Resources Blacksburg and New River Valley Current page: Greater Washington, D.C., area Roanoke Student Employment at Virginia Tech Virginia Tech Human Resources Greater Washington, D.C., area Virginia Tech's presence in the Greater Washington, D.C., area brings pioneering research and top-quality graduate programs to the modern metropolis of Northern Virginia. In the region since 1969, Virginia Tech has a long tradition of creating new knowledge and applying it to the critical problems facing the Washington, D.C. area, the Commonwealth of Virginia, the nation, and the world. Booming with economic success, Northern Virginia fosters a rich environment for professional development and outreach as well as entertainment and family fun. Quick Facts Virginia Tech offers more than 45 graduate degree and certificate programs, in the greater D.C. area, taught by internationally recognized faculty. The university's teaching locations, in Old Town Alexandria, the Virginia Tech Research Center - Arlington, and new academic building in Alexandria. Northern Virginia's transportation infrastructure includes the Metro and two major airports, Dulles International Airport and Reagan National Airport . In 2010, the greater D.C. area reported $10.9 million in sponsored research and the region’s outreach program provided noncredit educational services to 1,681 individuals. According to U.S. News & World Report , the top 10 schools in Virginia are all located in Northern Virginia. Relocation Resources The links found on this page are a small sampling of online resources that were curated to help with the process of moving to the area. It is important to note that this is not a comprehensive list, and we do not endorse non-Virginia Tech affiliates. Chamber and Community Websites Alexandria Chamber of Commerce Arlington Chamber of Commerce Fairfax County Chamber of Commerce Falls Church Chamber of Commerce Loudoun County Chamber of Commerce Prince William Chamber of Commerce Childcare Providers Visit the university's caregiving resources website . County/Town Websites City of Alexandria Arlington City of Fairfax The City of Falls Church The Town of Leesburg City of Manassas Town of Middleburg Medical Hospitals in Northern Virginia area Realtors Northern Virginia Association of Realtors Short-Term Leasing Short Term Lodging Source Short Term Rentals Email - VThousing@dweckproperties.com Email - Hokies@NationalCorporateHousing.com Schools Alexandria City Public Schools Arlington Public Schools Fairfax County Public Schools Falls Church City Public Schools Loudoun County Public Schools Manassas City Public Schools Social/Civic Culture Capital Connect with America: Fairfax, Virginia Washington, D.C. Professional Networking Transportation Commuter Choice Program (for Virginia Tech employees) Commuter Page Dulles International Airport Metro Metropolitan Washington Airports Authority Reagan National Airport Virginia Department of Rail and Public Transportation Workforce Development Offices Alexandria Virginia Employment Commission Prince William Virginia Employment Commission Division of Human Resources Talent Acquisition Team North End Center, Suite 2300 300 Turner Street NW Blacksburg, VA 24061 Hours Monday - Friday, 8 a.m.-5 p.m. Phone 540-231-9331 Fax 540-231-3830 Email recruiting@vt.edu Follow Us Facebook | X Get Directions See All Locations Contact Virginia Tech University Status Principles of Community Privacy Statement Acceptable Use We Remember University Libraries Accessibility Consumer Information Cost & Aid SAFE at VT Policies Equal Opportunity WVTF University Bookstore Jobs at Virginia Tech © 2026 Virginia Polytechnic Institute and State University. All rights reserved. Instagram Facebook Linked-In Threads Youtube X Blue Sky"
